{
  "case_id": "2008-08-322",
  "document_hash": "7d911784d986303b3f6041f9306619afee5efae5cb0bd5f36fbda4cd48545055",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Northwest Austin Municipal Utility District (Appellant)",
      "case_id": "2008-08-322",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d911784d986303b3f6041f9306619afee5efae5cb0bd5f36fbda4cd48545055",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d911784d986-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. COLEMAN: Good morning, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court:\nAfter more than 20 years of steadfast compliance with the Voting Rights Act, Northwest Austin MUD Number One is entitled to be free from the intrusive burdens of preclearance. The district is entitled to seek a bailout because it is a political subdivision under the Court's decisions in Sheffield and Dougherty County. This natural parallelism between bailout and preclearance allows bailout to serve its ameliorative purposes of encouraging, recognizing, and rewarding long-term compliance and progress --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-08-322",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d911784d986303b3f6041f9306619afee5efae5cb0bd5f36fbda4cd48545055",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d911784d986-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Bailout wasn't involved in those cases. And what do you do with a statute that has three categories -- the State, political subdivision, and then there's \"governmental unit\"? The district qualifies as a governmental unit. Why would Congress add that third category if the district came within \"political subdivision\"?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Coleman",
      "case_id": "2008-08-322",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d911784d986303b3f6041f9306619afee5efae5cb0bd5f36fbda4cd48545055",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d911784d986-0001-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "with respect to both black and Hispanic voters, the record in covered jurisdictions is above the national average."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Coleman",
      "case_id": "2008-08-322",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d911784d986303b3f6041f9306619afee5efae5cb0bd5f36fbda4cd48545055",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d911784d986-0001-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Massachusetts, for instance, you might be learned to know, has a white-black voter registration and turnout differential that is in the high 20s, far in excess of any covered jurisdiction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Coleman",
      "case_id": "2008-08-322",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d911784d986303b3f6041f9306619afee5efae5cb0bd5f36fbda4cd48545055",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d911784d986-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the only covered State would have been Hawaii. Under that formula, using modern data, modern information, none of these States would have been covered if you account for noncitizen voting age population."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Katyal",
      "case_id": "2008-08-322",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d911784d986303b3f6041f9306619afee5efae5cb0bd5f36fbda4cd48545055",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d911784d986-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "After 16,000 pages of testimony, 21 different hearings over 10 months, Congress looked at the evidence and determined that their work was not done."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Katyal",
      "case_id": "2008-08-322",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d911784d986303b3f6041f9306619afee5efae5cb0bd5f36fbda4cd48545055",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d911784d986-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "section 5 is actually working very well; that it provides a deterrent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Katyal",
      "case_id": "2008-08-322",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d911784d986303b3f6041f9306619afee5efae5cb0bd5f36fbda4cd48545055",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d911784d986-0001-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "they led the country in the number of objections. They found that the -- that the registration rates, as Justice Souter said, between Hispanics and whites was great."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-08-322",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d911784d986303b3f6041f9306619afee5efae5cb0bd5f36fbda4cd48545055",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d911784d986-0001-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Over a quarter of a century, there have been 15 bailouts that have gone through? All of them in the State of Virginia?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Katyal",
      "case_id": "2008-08-322",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d911784d986303b3f6041f9306619afee5efae5cb0bd5f36fbda4cd48545055",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d911784d986-0001-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There have been 18 under the new provision, which is --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-08-322",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d911784d986303b3f6041f9306619afee5efae5cb0bd5f36fbda4cd48545055",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d911784d986-0002-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It fends off Section 2 suits, I assume. I mean, that's great. You get a declaratory judgment, here -- you know, a benediction, and you skip off without having to face suits."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Katyal",
      "case_id": "2008-08-322",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d911784d986303b3f6041f9306619afee5efae5cb0bd5f36fbda4cd48545055",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d911784d986-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, I think that we shouldn't -- this Court should be loathe to second-guess the motivations of Congress under --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-08-322",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d911784d986303b3f6041f9306619afee5efae5cb0bd5f36fbda4cd48545055",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d911784d986-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Could I ask you this question about -- about bailout? I mean we have -- there's a very odd aspect to this case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-08-322",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d911784d986303b3f6041f9306619afee5efae5cb0bd5f36fbda4cd48545055",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d911784d986-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What I understand it, is this incorrect? As I understand it for Travis County to get a bailout, it would -- it has within Travis County something like 106 political subdivisions that are covered, and Travis County would have to go to all of those 106 and demonstrate that there has been no violation by any of those 106 for the preceding whatever it is, five years, whatever the bailout provision is."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Adegbile",
      "case_id": "2008-08-322",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d911784d986303b3f6041f9306619afee5efae5cb0bd5f36fbda4cd48545055",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d911784d986-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our long experience demonstrates that racial discrimination in voting has been persistent and adaptive."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Adegbile",
      "case_id": "2008-08-322",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d911784d986303b3f6041f9306619afee5efae5cb0bd5f36fbda4cd48545055",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d911784d986-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And as Appellants recognize in their brief, 600 -- notwithstanding the powerful section 5 remedy, there were 653 successful section 2 cases in covered jurisdictions, and the success rate in covered jurisdictions was much higher than in noncovered jurisdictions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-08-322",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d911784d986303b3f6041f9306619afee5efae5cb0bd5f36fbda4cd48545055",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d911784d986-0003-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the Constitution that section 5 is designed to implement covers only intentional discrimination."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2008-08-322",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d911784d986303b3f6041f9306619afee5efae5cb0bd5f36fbda4cd48545055",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d911784d986-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "How long did it take Congress to compile this 13,000-page record?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Gregory S. Coleman",
      "case_id": "2008-08-322",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d911784d986303b3f6041f9306619afee5efae5cb0bd5f36fbda4cd48545055",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d911784d986-0003-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But, as Justice Alito pointed out, Congress didn't know, because it didn't ask, whether discrimination is worse in Tennessee or Arkansas than in Virginia and other States. Nobody knows sitting here today."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-08-322",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d911784d986303b3f6041f9306619afee5efae5cb0bd5f36fbda4cd48545055",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d911784d986-0003-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, they now have 25 years to look at, or 24 years, to look at the rest of the country. Are they doing that? Are they holding hearings?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Gregory S. Coleman",
      "case_id": "2008-08-322",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d911784d986303b3f6041f9306619afee5efae5cb0bd5f36fbda4cd48545055",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d911784d986-0003-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "No, I don't think that's our argument. I think our argument is it's partially unconstitutional because it even failed to look at the coverage criteria and that it used the criteria literally off the books from the '60s and '70s without even looking at the information."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Gregory S. Coleman",
      "case_id": "2008-08-322",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d911784d986303b3f6041f9306619afee5efae5cb0bd5f36fbda4cd48545055",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d911784d986-0003-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But in terms of this facial challenge, it is important for the Court to understand and to consider the fact that Congress really thumbed its nose at the Court in terms of rejecting the constitutional concerns that the Court raised in -- in Miller and in Bossier Parish and in Georgia versus Ashcroft."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-08-322",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d911784d986303b3f6041f9306619afee5efae5cb0bd5f36fbda4cd48545055",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d911784d986-0003-0009",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2008-08-322",
      "confidence": 0.0,
